# Code quality (Finance)

Distilled from SteelMC / Kudu / Glowroot agent standards. Stack here: Vite + React + Hono + SQLite.

## Ask, don't guess

Ambiguity is a stop signal. If CSV format, category rules, KPI math, auth/deploy, or schema intent is unclear: ask. No speculative coding.

## Honest blockers

Don't hide uncertainty behind workarounds. State what you verified, what is missing, why guessing risks wrong money numbers / PII leaks / broken import, and the exact file/log/decision needed.

## Verify before asking

Inspect relevant parsers, `server/` routes, SQLite schema, fixtures, and tests first. If still blocked, say what you checked.

## Foundations

Don't land stubs or fake financial data in shared paths (`src/lib/*`, `server/lib/*`, schema) unless explicitly prototyping and labeled. Partial work must not break import/dedup/KPI for the rest of the app.

## Code standard

- Prefer small diffs; no new deps if a few lines suffice (`ponytail` + Karpathy).
- Guard clauses over deep nesting.
- Identifiers/comments English; UI strings Italian.
- After a fix, don't leave comments that only narrate the old bug.
- Don't multithread/async unless I/O needs it (API/quotes already async where required).

## Testing

- Test meaningful behavior (parser edge cases, stats/KPI, merge/dedup, portfolio math) — not coverage theater.
- After changes: narrowest check (`npm test` filter or full) that exercises touched code; then `npm run build` before done.
- Parser/CSV work: TDD on fixtures first.

## UI quality

- Preserve existing design system in `styles.css` (charcoal / teal / clay). No new UI kit.
- Layout changes: keep sidebar + tab patterns; visual smoke (Playwright MCP ok) when structure changes.
- Do not invent a second visual language (no purple gradients, cream-serif marketing look, or card spam) unless the user asks for a redesign.
- User-visible copy stays Italian and consistent with neighboring screens.

## Privacy / secrets

- Never commit real bank CSV, `data/*.db`, `.env`, Finnhub keys, or PII exports.
- Quote API keys stay server-side only (Settings → server), never in the Vite bundle.
